==============================================================================
A5. Paley tournament on F_7, independent recount
==============================================================================
arcs: 21 ; out-degrees: [3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3]
cyclic triples: 14 ; transitive: 21 ; regular-tournament formula C(7,3) - 7*C(3,2) = 14
cyc == dev{0,1,3} | dev{0,1,5}: True ; disjoint: True ; sizes 7 7
  dev{0,1,3}: every pair of points in exactly [1] block(s)
  dev{0,1,5}: every pair of points in exactly [1] block(s)
  union: every pair of points in exactly [2] block(s)
line rule dev{0,1,3}: s->s+1->s+3->s : True  (e_i e_{i+1} = e_{i+3})
line rule dev{0,1,5}: s->s+1->s+5->s : True  (differences 1, 4, 2 all in QR)
lines of dev{0,1,3} are themselves cyclic triples (identity map, injective): True
so 'the 7 lines map to 7 directed 3-cycle triads' is TRUE for one plane and INCOMPLETE (7 more cycles in dev{0,1,5});
'exactly 21 directed 3-cycles' stays false: 14 cycles, 42 rooted cycles, 21 = arcs = transitive triples.
h(T_7) by brute force over 5040 permutations = 189
189 is odd (Redei) and is neither 7 nor 21 (THM-1370-h-spectrum-omits-7-21-all-n.md).

